  "description": "Real Spanish names from INE records, with two surnames the Spanish way: father's then mother's. Castilian, Catalan, Basque and Galician first names.",
  "seoKeywords": "spanish name generator, spanish names, spanish last names, spanish surnames, spanish last name generator, spanish surname generator, spanish girl names, spanish boy names, spanish female names, spanish male names, random spanish name, random spanish name generator, spanish full name generator, spanish first names, common spanish surnames, spanish names with two last names, spanish double surnames, spanish names for characters, catalan names, basque names, galician names",
  "isPopular": false,
  "noun": "Spanish Names",
  "noEcho": true,
  "capitalise": true,
  "nameSource": {
    "kind": "recorded",
    "note": "Every first name and surname is real, from INE, Spain's national statistics institute (Apellidos y nombres más frecuentes). First names are the most frequent names of people born in Spain, decade by decade and province by province (Padrón, 1 January 2022), kept if at least 1,500 people in Spain have them. Surnames are the most frequent first surnames of people born in each province (Censos anuales, 1 January 2025). INE publishes names without accents or particles, so the accents are added back and compound names like María del Carmen, which can't be rebuilt for sure, are left out. Source: own work with data from the INE website, www.ine.es, reused under CC BY 4.0. The names are joined at random, so a full name is a new pairing. Surnames that are also brands or first names, such as Ferrero and Juan, are kept; a few whose usual written form is unclear are left out, and pairings that match a famous person, such as Fernando Alonso or Pedro Sánchez, are blocked."
  },
